t reads  be a voice for justice Archie it's just  five months old is being kept in their  official residence under the safe and  watchful eye of his nanny next to the  Sussex is visited the district six  museum in Cape Town which celebrates the  once lively multiracial area that was  destroyed during apartheid back in the  60s and 70s  Megan flipped into a sky blue  button-down dress for the occasion the  same one she sported during last year's  royal tour of the Pacific afterwards  they attended a cooking demonstration  and dinner at the homecoming Center the  Royals will spend the next few days in  Cape Town before Harry heads north to  Botswana Angola and Malawi Megan and  Archie will remain in South Africa the  places that Harry is visiting are simply  too remote and potentially too dangerous  for such a small baby malaria for  example is rife in some of the areas  that Harry will be visiting and the trio  will all reunite in Johannesburg for the  final two days of the tour which ends  October 2nd
 

